WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:07.000
HL: "Do you think our home is ready&nbsp;
to welcome our baby?"

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.400
Glo: "I mean,&nbsp;we can worry about that 
when the time&nbsp;comes."

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.400
HL: "But, isn't that like anytime now?"

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.080
Glo: "Oh s*** ..."

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.240
Yep, time really flies. This will be&nbsp;
our last video before our baby arrives.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.640
In fact, by the time you're watching&nbsp;
this, our family could very well have welcomed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:37.600
its newest member. But, as of right now,&nbsp;
we still have a huge problem. Our home is far from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:43.120
ready to house this new member, and we urgently&nbsp;
need to get it sorted out. So, we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:49.120
two objectives for this video. We need to rethink&nbsp;
the layout of our home because the current layout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:55.120
isn't going to work, and we'll have to add more&nbsp;
storage. On top of that, we still want our home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:03.800
to retain its identity of being minimal&nbsp;
and modular. Is that a little too much to ask?

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.920
Over the years, we've heard this sentiment&nbsp;
countless times. Our home will be useless when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:22.880
we have kids. But, that's kind of a silly thing&nbsp;
to say as that would be like saying a bicycle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:30.320
is useless because it's not a family sedan. We&nbsp;
originally designed our home for just the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:37.440
of us, so we kind of get the point. The&nbsp;
old layout isn't the most ideal for raising kids.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:44.800
But, one of the advantages of having what&nbsp;
some might call an unfurnished home is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:51.280
we can adapt relatively easily. So, that's what&nbsp;
we're going to do. Or I should say, that's what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:57.840
Glo's going to do since I'm like a queen now,&nbsp;
and a queen doesn't do any of this grunt work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:04.000
Let's first switch our rooms around so our baby&nbsp;
will actually have somewhere to sleep.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:26.400
On a side note, we also want to talk a little&nbsp;
about minimalism in the context of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:32.400
parenthood. Because apparently, what we've&nbsp;
gathered is that once you have kids, it becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:40.160
impossible to be minimalist. Now, everyone has&nbsp;
their own definition of minimalism. To some,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:46.640
we are not minimalist at all, and to others, we&nbsp;
might come across as too minimalist. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:53.040
that's perfectly fine. We've never placed much&nbsp;
weight on the label. Our definition of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:03:00.880
minimalism is simply intentional living grounded&nbsp;
in self-honesty. We want to consciously choose the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:07.840
things that would genuinely make our lives rich,&nbsp;
and we strive to examine those choices as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:14.000
honestly as we can. Which means that by our&nbsp;
definition, it's not the amount of things we own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:22.360
that define us. We are happy as long as we live&nbsp;
intentionally and examine our choices truthfully.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.480
Maybe what people mean when they say you&nbsp;
can't be a minimalist once you have kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:38.320
is that you can no longer look minimalist. And&nbsp;
that may very well be true. Babies don't care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:45.200
about the aesthetic that we've created, so I'm&nbsp;
sure things will get messy once our baby arrives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:53.360
But to us, minimalism is not an aesthetic or&nbsp;
a binary outcome. Instead, it's a process,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:04:00.160
a continual practice of being intentional&nbsp;
and honest. And this process becomes even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:06.960
more important once kids come into the&nbsp;
picture, life will become more chaotic and we will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:14.000
have more things. Instead of becoming another&nbsp;
impossible standard to live up to, ideally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:21.680
minimalism should serve us and make life with&nbsp;
kids feel simpler. The question is, can we remain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:27.040
intentional when life gets more complicated?&nbsp;
And that's what we'll find out soon enough.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:39.920
Back to the state of our home for a moment. Over&nbsp;
the years, we've learned a lot about the things we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:47.360
need and how much storage space would be optimal&nbsp;
for the two of us. But now, we have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:53.760
prepare for a whole new person whose habits and&nbsp;
needs are still completely unknown. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:05:00.720
we can only make an educated guess as we add&nbsp;
more storage to each of our rooms. But at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:08.320
same time, we also want to reuse as much of&nbsp;
our existing stuff as we can to reduce waste.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:16.160
For example here, although we went with a new PAX&nbsp;
wardrobe, we specifically planned on combining it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:22.480
with our old pull-out storage boxes.&nbsp;
And we're pretty happy with how it turned out.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:42.320
As a first-time mother, it's so easy to feel&nbsp;
overwhelmed. Of course, it's always good to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:47.200
slightly over prepared than under prepared.&nbsp;
But there are so many different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:54.560
opinions on what a baby needs and there are&nbsp;
endless baby essentials lists on the internet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:59.840
which sometimes makes us wonder how many&nbsp;
of the things we think we need are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:06.800
truly essential. And how much of those are&nbsp;
a result of peer pressure, social pressure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:13.760
or good marketing. Are we just conditioned to&nbsp;
believe that because other happy babies all use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:21.600
certain products, we too must acquire more&nbsp;
and better things so our baby can be happy?

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:30.560
So, I decided I wanted to approach this with&nbsp;
a simpler mindset. We don't have to prepare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:37.200
for every outcome. All a baby needs&nbsp;
in the beginning is a safe place to sleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:45.440
clothes to wear, a well-fed belly, and&nbsp;
most importantly, lots of love. For now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:52.320
I think we have got those taken care of. We&nbsp;
can figure out the rest along the way. 

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:15.200
All things considered, we are probably overstocked&nbsp;
and overprepared. One of the advantages of being a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:22.160
bit late to parenthood is that we have many peers&nbsp;
ahead of us to learn from and to receive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:28.720
plenty of hand-me-downs from, which we honestly&nbsp;
don't mind. A baby grows so fast, so many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:34.880
of the items will only be used for a few months&nbsp;
and then it'll be our turn to pass them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:42.160
on to the next pair of overwhelmed parents-to-be.&nbsp;
In the end, I think we managed to retain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:48.960
much of our home's personality. Everything is&nbsp;
still modular and movable, ready to adapt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:55.440
further changes in our lives. And we are also&nbsp;
ready to have more things. The material outcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.440 --> 00:08:02.480
of owning as little as possible has never been the&nbsp;
goal for us. We've always been more interested in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:08.320
the process and the journey itself. And there&nbsp;
hasn't been a journey we've looked forward to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:14.120
more than the one that lies ahead, even if&nbsp;
it means having a little more mess at home.

